Made by gen_bittensor_fetch.py (in the shared notes folder) with Python 3.14.4, bittensor 11.1.0, aiohttp 3.13.5 and lxml 6.1.1, PYTHONPATH a feat/bulk-bittensor checkout. vectors.json: `vectors`, yarl's URL(), str() and join(), urljoin, and RobotFileParser's can_fetch and crawl_delay on hand-picked cases. chain/: the JSON-RPC answers of a `bulk bittensor-fetch --only-chain --block 9491485` run recorded through examples/rpc_record.rs, each block cut to its first extrinsic (`chain-fixture`), and python/, bittensor_fetch.chain_snapshot with client.block pinned to 9491485 then registration_dates, written as fetch() writes them. replay/: the HTTP exchanges of a live Python fetch of subnets 2, 6, 20, 39, 45, 50, 101, 120, 122 and 128 on 2026-11-12 (`record`), with blocks cut to their first extrinsic and synthetic hosts and subnets 900-904 added (`replay-fixture`); input/ holds the chain snapshot and a synthetic previous fetch; python/ and stdout.txt: the Python fetch run against examples/fetch_replay.rs serving replay.json.gz (`replay`), from a folder holding input/previous as previous.
